#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:25
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:27
msgid ""
"`nix profile` allows you to create and manage _Nix profiles_. A Nix profile "
"is a set of packages that can be installed and upgraded independently from "
"each other. Nix profiles are versioned, allowing them to be rolled back "
"easily."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:32
msgid "Files"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:34
msgid "Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:36
msgid ""
"A directory that contains links to profiles managed by [`nix-env`](../../"
"command-ref/nix-env.md) and [`nix profile`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-"
"profile.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:38
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles` for regular users"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:39
msgid "`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root` if the user is `root`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:41
msgid "A profile is a directory of symlinks to files in the Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:43
msgid "Filesystem layout"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:45
msgid ""
"Profiles are versioned as follows. When using a profile named _path_, _path_ "
"is a symlink to _path_`-`_N_`-link`, where _N_ is the version of the "
"profile. In turn, _path_`-`_N_`-link` is a symlink to a path in the Nix "
"store. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:57
msgid "Each of these symlinks is a root for the Nix garbage collector."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:59
msgid ""
"The contents of the store path corresponding to each version of the profile "
"is a tree of symlinks to the files of the installed packages, e.g."
msgstr ""

