msgid "Each profile version contains a manifest file:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:87
msgid ""
"[`manifest.nix`](../../command-ref/files/manifest.nix.md) used by [`nix-env`]"
"(../../command-ref/nix-env.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:88
msgid ""
"[`manifest.json`](../../command-ref/files/manifest.json.md) used by [`nix "
"profile`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md) (experimental)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:90
msgid "User profile link"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:92
msgid "A symbolic link to the user's current profile:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:94
msgid "`~/.nix-profile`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:95
msgid ""
"`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profile` if [`use-xdg-base-directories`](../../command-"
"ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-directories) is set to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:97
msgid "By default, this symlink points to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:99
msgid "`$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles/profile` for regular users"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:100
msgid "`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root/profile` for `root`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:102
msgid ""
"The `PATH` environment variable should include `/bin` subdirectory of the "
"profile link (e.g. `~/.nix-profile/bin`) for the user environment to be "
"visible to the user. The [installer](../../installation/installing-binary."
"md) sets this up by default, unless you enable [`use-xdg-base-directories`]"
"(../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-directories)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:109
msgid "Profile compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:111
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:128
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:113
msgid ""
"Once you have used [`nix profile`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile."
"md) you can no longer use [`nix-env`](../../command-ref/nix-env.md) without "
"first deleting `$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles/profile`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:118
msgid ""
"Once you installed a package with [`nix profile`](../../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix3-profile.md), you get the following error message when using [`nix-env`]"
"(../../command-ref/nix-env.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:126
msgid "To migrate back to `nix-env` you can delete your current profile:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:130
msgid ""
"This will delete packages that have been installed before, so you may want "
"to back up this information before running the command."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md:132
msgid ""
"```console\n"
" $ rm -rf \"${XDG_STATE_HOME-$HOME/.local/state}/nix/profiles/profile\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

